     1	"""Value-gap diagnostic driver (run statement
     2	ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/run-statements/value-gap-diagnostic.md).
     3	
     4	Two streams in parallel, each in a worker thread: GPU 0 runs the Kaggriculture
     5	stages (kg_gap.py), GPU 1 the Isaiah control (is_gap.py). Every stage is a fresh
     6	subprocess in its own session with its own Inductor/Triton cache. The driver
     7	stops at the FIRST unexpected failure (nonzero exit, timeout, missing/errored
     8	result, a step not ok, a wrong/missing backend record, a non-finite comparison,
     9	wrong use_flash_attn flags, wrong compiled-trunk call count): the other
    10	stream's running stage is terminated and nothing further starts. Gap sizes are
    11	results, never failures.
    12	
    13	Exit codes: 0 all non-optional stages ran and passed; 3 a stage failed; 4 the
    14	internal deadline ran out; 128 + signum on SIGTERM/SIGINT/SIGHUP (cleanup ran).
    15	
    16	Process-group cleanup. Adapted from kg/rebuild-gpu-checks 6392160 driver.py,
    17	with the spawn/registration gap of Codex review verify-gpu-bundle-r2 finding 3
    18	closed structurally:
    19	  * stages are spawned only from worker threads; CPython runs the Python-level
    20	    signal handler only in the main thread, which never spawns and only joins;
    21	  * Popen and registration happen under self.spawn_lock (non-reentrant), which
    22	    the handler also takes before snapshotting the groups, so a group is either
    23	    registered before cleanup snapshots or is never created (a worker checks
    24	    self.cleaned under the lock before Popen);
    25	  * cleanup: SIGTERM each started group, wait <= TERM_GRACE_S, SIGKILL the
    26	    survivors, wait <= KILL_GRACE_S; total below launch.sh's `-k 20` grace.
    27	
    28	VGAP_DRIVER_SELFTEST=<dir> replaces the stages by dummy CPU sleep stages (see
    29	test_driver_cleanup.py); it is for the local cleanup test only.
